# What the install medium's mfsroot holds (OxideBSD-doc INSTALLER.md §4.2), one path a line: a
# path marked `rescue` is a hard link to /rescue/rescue, the tools crunched into one program
# (rescue/, which must include it); any other is taken from the installed tree. build_install.rs
# makes target/images/mfsroot.img of them, their directories, and this directory's etc/, which
# replaces the tree's files of the same names.
# The image stays in RAM all the while the medium runs, so only what installing and repairing need:
# every byte here is a byte less for a 64 MB machine.
./bin/cat	rescue
./bin/chmod	rescue
./bin/cp	rescue
./bin/date	rescue
./bin/dd	rescue
./bin/df	rescue
